{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"d85df717-0f3b-4a6f-9848-07cc1270d896","title":"Doppler effect with circular wavefronts"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d85df717-0f3b-4a6f-9848-07cc1270d896","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A source moves right while sound spreads outward at speed c. This oldest wavefront stays centered where it was emitted, not on the moving source.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Doppler effect: moving source"},{"op":"figure","id":"waves","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-4.6,4.8],"y":[-4.5,4.5],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"old","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"circle","id":"outer","center":{"at":"old"},"r":4},{"kind":"point","id":"source","at":[2.4,0],"label":"source"},{"kind":"segment","from":[2.4,0.4],"to":[3.3,0.4],"arrow":true,"label":"vₛ"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"condition","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"0<v_s<c"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d85df717-0f3b-4a6f-9848-07cc1270d896","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Successive crests are emitted one period apart. Their centers shift right, so the circular wavefronts bunch ahead and spread apart behind.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"morewaves","on":"waves","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"center2","at":[0.6,0]},{"kind":"circle","id":"wave2","center":{"at":"center2"},"r":3},{"kind":"point","id":"center3","at":[1.2,0]},{"kind":"circle","id":"wave3","center":{"at":"center3"},"r":2},{"kind":"point","id":"center4","at":[1.8,0]},{"kind":"circle","id":"wave4","center":{"at":"center4"},"r":1}]},{"op":"equation","id":"period","anchor":{"el":"condition","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"T=\\frac{1}{f_s},\\qquad \\Delta x_{\\text{source}}=v_sT"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d85df717-0f3b-4a6f-9848-07cc1270d896","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Ahead, each wavelength is shortened by the source's travel during one period. A stationary listener receives more crests per second: higher frequency.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"frontgap","on":"waves","marks":[{"kind":"measure","from":[3.6,0],"to":[4,0],"label":"λ ahead"},{"kind":"text","at":[3.5,-1.4],"text":"higher pitch","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"ahead","anchor":{"el":"period","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\lambda_{\\text{ahead}}=(c-v_s)T\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad f_{\\text{ahead}}=f_s\\frac{c}{c-v_s}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"d85df717-0f3b-4a6f-9848-07cc1270d896","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s4"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d85df717-0f3b-4a6f-9848-07cc1270d896","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Behind, the crests are farther apart, giving lower frequency. The wave speed remains c; changed spacing causes the pitch shift for stationary listeners.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"backgap","on":"waves","marks":[{"kind":"measure","from":[-4,0],"to":[-2.4,0],"label":"λ behind"},{"kind":"text","at":[-2.9,-1.4],"text":"lower pitch","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"behind","anchor":{"el":"ahead","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\lambda_{\\text{behind}}=(c+v_s)T\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad f_{\\text{behind}}=f_s\\frac{c}{c+v_s}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
